  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_042: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.6352) establishes that multi-profile + ViT-L + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest combination. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as pca_n2000 in this setting, while scvi_n200 remains completely untested. In single-profile settings, scgpt underperformed pca_n2000 (0.4214 vs 0.5232), but scvi_n200 is a different learned representation that has not been evaluated. Config_047 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding all other hyperparameters at their best-known values, cleanly isolating the effect of the RNA representation. This is the highest-value next experiment because it tests the single most important unexplored design axis in the current best region, and the result will determine whether further investment should go toward learned RNA encoders or toward other dimensions (aggregation, fusion) with PCA fixed."
